LanguageData.RP_OverdoseText:
{0} overdosed on the wing. The others watched it happen.

{1}

Go after the supply, get {0} help (tension down, and a referral to substance abuse treatment - first seat at the next session), or note it in the file and move on.

LanguageData.RP_InnocenceText:
{0}, {2} days into a sentence for {1}, has written to you. They didn't do it, and they want the warden's support for an appeal.

{3}

Back the appeal and the court will take it seriously. If {0} is innocent, they will very likely walk free. If they are not, the parole board will remember that you vouched for them. Stay out of it and {0} fights alone.

LanguageData.RP_FoodScareText:
{1} inmates are doubled over after the last meal: {0}. The infirmary says food poisoning, and the wings say the kitchen is trying to kill them.

{2}

You can close the kitchen for a scrub ({3} - every bit of filth goes, and it ends there), stand the inmate kitchen crew down for {4} hours (the staff cook meanwhile, and a second wave is less likely), or carry on serving and hope it was a bad batch - a second wave within the day is likely, more so in a dirty kitchen.

LanguageData.RP_Alert_ReferralBlockedDesc:
Inmates you referred to a program are waiting because their class cannot start:

{0}

Fix it on the Programs screen (the Policy button, Programs tab; a room with seats or space, a teacher on site, or switch the program on); a class that only waits for a room or teacher another program is using needs a second room or teacher.

LanguageData.RP_MeasuresText:
{0}

The state has put the prison under special measures. The overseer, {2}, will review it in {1} days. Three targets must be met by then. {6}

Until the review the state caps the shuttle at {3} new inmates a day, pays {4} less for every inmate, keeps armed guards from firing on rioters, sells no land and caps solitary at {5} hours (lighter sanctions are not capped). Meet the targets and the measures are lifted with a grant. Miss them and the term is extended once, with no new inmates sent at all. Miss them again and the state installs a security chief of its own, and the restrictions stay for as long as the chief does.

This is part of the game's difficulty and is always on.

LanguageData.RP_MeasuresExtendedText:
The overseer, {0}, has reviewed the prison and the targets were not met. The measures run for another {1} days, and from now on the state sends no new inmates at all.

{2}

If the next review goes the same way, the state installs a security chief of its own and the bureaucracy loses its latest project ({3}). You can ask for the chief now instead, but that gains nothing. The term ends at once, the restrictions stay, and the chief and the lost project come with it. Unanswered, the term simply runs on.

LanguageData.RP_Alert_MeasuresDesc:
The overseer reviews the prison in {0} days.

{1}

Until then the shuttle's new inmates are {2}, inmate payments are cut by {3}, armed response is held at escapes only and solitary is capped at {4} hours.

LanguageData.RP_TrialAssembledText:
The prosecution has assembled its case against {0} for the murder of {1}. The trial is set for {2}.

{3}

On what the prosecution has, the case looks {4}. Witnesses can still be got at before the day, and a case can still be made stronger.

LanguageData.RP_TrialConvictedText:
The trial of {0} for the murder of {1} was held {2}. {0} was found guilty. The sentence is {3}, and {0} goes to maximum security if there is room.

What came out in court
{4}

LanguageData.RP_TrialAcquittedText:
The trial of {0} for the murder of {1} was held {2}. {0} was acquitted. Nothing is added to their sentence, and {1}'s friends and gang want revenge.

What came out in court
{3}
